resultJson.description:
Add Grok Build (`grok`, xAI's coding-agent CLI) as orca's sixth backend: a new `grok/` module (`orca-grok`, package `orca.tools.grok`) with `BackendTag.Grok` and settings harness name `grok`. After this, `codingAgent = grok` or `grok:<model>` works in settings files, flows get a `grok` accessor, and the shell supports grok for `orca continue`, the flow-authoring slug and the wizard. Grok also gets a row in the AGENTS.md enforcement table. The design is already researched and committed. `INTEGRATE_GROK_BUILD.md` covers the invocation, ClientClaimed sessions, the tool-tier mapping, `--json-schema`, `ask_user` over MCP through a temp `--agent` file, models, the proposed enforcement row and the open questions. `HARNESS_INTEGRATION_GUIDE.md` covers the AgentBackend/LineDecoder contract, the registration touchpoints (§7) and the testing expectations (§8). Implementers follow these documents instead of re-deriving the design.

Grok's `--output-format streaming-messages-json` is Claude Code's stream-json wire format. So the central refactor is to move claude's stream-json decoding (`InboundMessage`, `ContentBlock`, `StreamEventPayload` and the decoder fold) out of the claude module into one shared decoder in `tools`, parameterized by a small dialect. Claude and grok each instantiate it. Claude's behaviour and all its tests must stay exactly as they are. The grok dialect handles the differences listed in the design doc's §3:
- the `ask_user` echo arrives as `use_tool` with `input.tool_name == "orca__ask_user"`;
- failure messages include the result's `errors[]`;
- grok's refusal texts become `ToolDenied`;
- a model of `"unknown"` becomes None;
- an all-zero usage is treated as unobserved rather than a measured zero.

Enforcement follows the doc's §9: every tier is Hard except `Full, Only(_)`, which is Ignored (option B, `--always-approve`). Every read-only or no-tools argv must render a non-empty `--tools` list of real tool names, because an empty or unknown-only list silently disables filtering. Tests must pin that.

A logged-in `grok` 1.0.41 is on PATH. Use it to settle the doc's cheap open questions (§11), always with `-m grok-4.7-build-fast`, short prompts and only a handful of calls. Record the results back into `INTEGRATE_GROK_BUILD.md`, marked verified with the CLI version and date. Add a gated `GrokIntegrationTest` (`ORCA_INTEGRATION=1`) and run it once at the end. Do not push, open PRs or change remotes. Do not invent pricing rows: if `DefaultModelsPricedTest` needs grok coverage, leave a clearly marked TODO instead of guessed rates.

tasks.description:
Pure refactor, no behaviour change. Move `InboundMessage`, `ContentBlock` and `StreamEventPayload` from `claude/src/main/scala/orca/tools/claude/streamjson/` into a new package in tools, e.g. `tools/src/main/scala/orca/backend/messagesjson/` (package `orca.backend.messagesjson`, visibility `private[orca]`). Move their tests too (`ContentBlockTest`, `InboundMessageTest`, `StreamEventPayloadTest`), under `tools/src/test/scala/orca/backend/messagesjson/`. `OutboundMessage` stays in claude: it is claude-only stdin input.

Turn the body of `ClaudeDecoder` into a generic `MessagesJsonDecoder[B <: BackendTag](dialect: MessagesJsonDialect, outputSchema: Option[String]) extends LineDecoder[B, MessagesJsonDecoder.State]`, with the `State` case class moving along (keep its scaladoc). Give `MessagesJsonDialect` only what claude needs today:
- `backendName: String`, which also replaces the hard-coded "claude" in failure and control-request texts;
- `isAskUserCall(name: String, rawInput: String): Boolean`;
- `structuredOutputToolName: Option[String]`;
- `refusedTool(content: String): Option[String]`.

Also add a generic turn-start helper so a backend can replace `ClaudeTurn.apply` with one line.

Claude then becomes an instantiation. A `ClaudeDialect` (or a val in `ClaudeBackend`) uses `ClaudeBackend.AskUserToolName`, `StructuredOutputToolName` and `PermissionRefusal.toolName`. `ClaudeDecoder`/`ClaudeTurn` stay as thin wrappers, so `ClaudeTurnTest`, `ClaudeBackendTest` and `ClaudeIntegrationTest` compile unchanged, or with import-only edits. Update the stale `ClaudeDecoder.assistantMessage` reference in `tools/src/main/scala/orca/backend/ObservedTurn.scala`'s scaladoc. Also update the comment on the `chimp` dependency in `build.sbt` if it lists consumers.

Acceptance: `sbt tools/test claude/test` is green, with every claude test still asserting the same things. No new mutable state.

Docs only. Work through the Docs bullet of `HARNESS_INTEGRATION_GUIDE.md` §7:
- `README.md`: prerequisites, harness list, flow accessor table (`grok`), per-backend notes (ClientClaimed; hard `--tools` tiers; `Full, Only` widened to `--always-approve`; `ask_user` via a temp `--agent` file; cost reported by the CLI), the settings `harness` list, the `agent.cheap` mapping (`grok-4.7-build-fast`), and the `.fast` tier extension.
- `AGENTS.md`:
  - module layout line 21 (`claude/ codex/ gemini/ grok/ opencode/ pi/`);
  - the dependency graph, if any;
  - the `IdScheme` examples at ~lines 127 and 496 (grok is `ClientClaimed`);
  - the hand-maintained NetworkOnly grant list at ~line 256: add "grok: `web_search`, `web_fetch` on `--tools`";
  - the "what a run writes to disk" table (~line 315): grok writes only `$TMPDIR` temp prompt/agent files, nothing in the user tree. Say so if the table lists per-backend rows;
  - a mention that the shared stream-json decoder now lives in `tools/.../backend/messagesjson/`.
  - The enforcement table was already regenerated. Re-run `EnforcementTableTest` to confirm it is still current.
- `CONTRIBUTING.md`: the integration suites list (`GrokIntegrationTest`, needs a logged-in `grok`, and which env var overrides its model), and the published artifacts (`orca-grok`).
- `skills/orca/README.md`: add grok wherever harnesses are listed.
- `adr/0021-orca-shell.md`: add grok's row to the resume table (`grok --resume <wireId>`, cwd = workDir).
- Consider a short new ADR (next free number after 0024, modelled on `adr/0015-gemini-stream-json-driver.md`) recording the grok driver and the shared messages-json decoder. Link it from `INTEGRATE_GROK_BUILD.md`.

Acceptance: `grep -ri gemini` over README/AGENTS/CONTRIBUTING/skills shows no harness list that is missing grok, and `sbt runner/testOnly orca.runner.EnforcementTableTest` is green.
